# The scaling of a ball with 2-limb center by a positive power of two c, with the special states of
# a ball: ball_mul_pow2_2, then the fix-up of ball_scale_2_full (milestone2.md, "Scaling a ball by
# a power of two"; milestone1.md, "Ball kernels"). One ball operand, so q is rx itself; |cz0| is
# named az, as in ball_scale_2_full. The whole line when the scaled center or radius overflows.
# finite_when (statement B4): the result is a finite ball when no member of the operand times c
# exceeds a quarter of the overflow threshold in magnitude, (|cx| + rx) c <= 2^(emax - 2).
# exact_when: a finite result under the conditions of the core is c X exactly.
kernel:        ball_mul_pow2_2_full
input:         cx = cx0 cx1
input:         stored rx
input:         c
output:        cw = cw0 cw1
output:        rw
value:         cx*c
requires:      ball cx rx
requires:      power_of_two c
ensures:       encloses cw rw x*c x=cx,rx finite_when=abs_le((abs(cx)+rx)*c,-2) exact_when=zero_or_abs_gt(cx[0]*c,eta/(2*u));zero_or_abs_gt(cx[1]*c,eta/(2*u));zero_or_abs_gt(rx*c,eta/(2*u))
min_precision: 2
source:        ball_mul_pow2_2, then the fix-up of the special states of a ball (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       core: as ball_mul_pow2_2; fix-up: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeBallPow2.v ball_mul_pow2_2_full_correct
entry:         yes
ieee_only:     yes
cone_exempt:   the fix-up selects, after explicit tests that the center and the radius are finite (f) and that the operand is not empty (e); B1 to B4 of milestone1.md, "Ball kernels", state what comes out

(cz0, cz1, rz) = ball_mul_pow2_2(cx0, cx1, rx, c)
e              = eq(rx, rx)
az             = abs(cz0)
f1             = lt(az, const inf)
f2             = lt(rz, const inf)
f              = and(f1, f2)
c0             = select(f, cz0, 0)
c1             = select(f, cz1, 0)
r              = select(f, rz, const inf)
cw0            = select(e, c0, rx)
cw1            = select(e, c1, rx)
rw             = select(e, r, rx)
